<%# The AIsuru side of the demo. Everything here happens on the platform,
    not in this app: the app only downloads the prompts and shows the two
    agents side by side once the steps below have been carried out. %>

<div class="row mb-4" id="setup-guide">
  <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
    <div class="card shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-header text-white d-flex align-items-center" style="background: #6f42c1;">
        <i class="bi bi-list-check me-2"></i>
        <h5 class="mb-0">Step-by-step guide</h5>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">

        <%# Step 1 - download the prompts %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #6c757d;">1</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Download the two agent prompts</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              Two ready-made system prompts: an <strong>Expert</strong> that knows a fictional company
              policy, and an <strong>Assistant</strong> that knows nothing about it. The figures in the
              Expert are invented on purpose, because a real regulation would already be known to the
              model, and the demo would prove nothing.
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <%= link_to demo5_prompt_path(agent: "expert"), class: "btn btn-sm text-white", style: "background: #6f42c1;" do %>
                <i class="bi bi-download me-1"></i> Agent A: Expert prompt
              <% end %>
              <%= link_to demo5_prompt_path(agent: "assistant"), class: "btn btn-sm text-white", style: "background: #0d6efd;" do %>
                <i class="bi bi-download me-1"></i> Agent B: Assistant prompt
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Step 2 - create the agents %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #6c757d;">2</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Create the two agents in AIsuru</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
              Go to <a href="https://www.aisuru.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AIsuru</a> and create
              two agents. Paste each downloaded prompt into the corresponding agent's system prompt.
              Keep them clearly named, because you will be switching between them throughout the demo.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Step 3 - load them here %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #6c757d;">3</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Load both agents at the bottom of this page</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
              Scroll down to <a href="#load-agents">Load the two agents</a> and fill in the
              <strong>Memori (Agent) ID</strong> and <strong>Owner user ID</strong> of each one, exactly
              as in the other course demos. Both chats then appear side by side, and you run the rest of
              the demo without leaving this page.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Step 4 - baseline %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #0d6efd;">4</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Ask the Assistant first: the "before"</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
              With no MCP connected yet, ask agent B in the right-hand chat:
              <em>"What is the meal reimbursement cap for a business trip?"</em>
              It cannot know: the answer lives only in ACME's fictional policy. Either it says so,
              or it makes a number up. Both outcomes are the baseline you compare against at step 7.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Step 5 - expose the Expert as MCP %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #6f42c1;">5</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Turn the Expert into an MCP server</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-2">In AIsuru, open <strong>agent A</strong> and follow this exact path:</p>
            <ol class="text-muted mb-3">
              <li>Open the <strong>MCP</strong> section of the agent.</li>
              <li>Look for <strong>AIsuru Agent Link</strong> among the available MCPs.</li>
              <li>Click <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
              <li>In the window that opens, click <strong>Create MCP</strong>.</li>
              <li>
                <strong>AIsuru Agent Link</strong> now appears under the <strong>connected MCPs</strong>.
                Open its <strong>dashboard</strong>.
              </li>
              <li>
                At the bottom of the dashboard, click <strong>new token</strong>. Leave the type on
                <strong>Consumer</strong> and the token is created. <strong>Copy it.</strong>
              </li>
              <li>
                Scroll back to the top of the dashboard and copy the
                <strong>public MCP endpoint</strong> too, since step 6 needs both values.
              </li>
            </ol>

            <p class="text-muted mb-2">The token type is the whole point of this step:</p>
            <div class="table-responsive">
              <table class="table table-bordered table-sm">
                <thead class="table-light">
                  <tr>
                    <th style="width: 160px;">Token type</th>
                    <th>What it allows</th>
                    <th style="width: 110px;">Used in</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="fw-bold">Consumer</td>
                    <td>Query the agent as a tool. It answers, nothing else changes.</td>
                    <td>Step 6</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="fw-bold">Builder</td>
                    <td>
                      Everything the Consumer token allows, <strong>plus</strong> modifying the agent
                      including its prompt.
                    </td>
                    <td>Step 8</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="alert alert-warning py-2 small mb-0">
              <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>
              The Builder token contains the Consumer one. Handing it out when only querying is needed
              gives away the ability to rewrite the agent. Start with the narrower token and widen only
              when the task requires it.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Step 6 - register it on the Assistant %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #0d6efd;">6</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Register it as a custom MCP on the Assistant</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-2">Now open <strong>agent B</strong>:</p>
            <ol class="text-muted mb-0">
              <li>Open its <strong>MCP</strong> section.</li>
              <li>Among the available MCPs, choose <strong>add custom MCP</strong>.</li>
              <li>
                Fill in a <strong>name</strong> and a short <strong>description</strong> (this is what
                agent B sees when deciding whether to use the tool, so make it say it answers company
                policy questions), the <strong>authentication token</strong> and the <strong>URL</strong>:
                the Consumer token and the public MCP endpoint you copied at step 5.
              </li>
              <li>Create the MCP.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Step 7 - the after %>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #0d6efd;">7</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Ask again: the "after"</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
              Same question as step 4, same right-hand chat. This time the exact figure comes back. Ask
              the Expert on the left the same thing and compare: same source, one agent away.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-warning py-2 small">
          <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>
          Before step 8, keep a copy of agent A's current prompt somewhere safe. If the Builder-token
          edit replaces it instead of appending to it, that copy is the only way to restore the
          Expert's policy figures.
        </div>

        <%# Step 8 - builder token %>
        <div class="d-flex">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
            <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #d63384;">8</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h6 class="fw-bold">Swap in a Builder token and let B rewrite A</h6>
            <p class="text-muted mb-2">
              Go back to agent A's <strong>AIsuru Agent Link</strong> dashboard and create another token,
              this time choosing <strong>Builder</strong> instead of Consumer. Copy it, then edit the
              custom MCP you registered on agent B and replace the token with this one.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">
              Now ask B: <em>"Add a foreign travel rule to the policies: 90 euro per day cap."</em>
              B edits the Expert's own prompt. Hit <strong>Reload</strong> in the header of the left panel,
              since the open session still runs on the old prompt, then ask A about foreign
              travel. The rule is there. One agent just reconfigured another.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
